# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Runtime artifacts
*.log
*.tmp

# Backup archives (use git history instead)
*.zip

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local-only context / scratch. Working notes, not project documentation --
# docs/PIPELINE.md and the READMEs are the shared record. Remove this line if
# you decide these should be shared.
.context/

# Editor configuration is per-developer.
.vscode/

# The corpus lives on Hugging Face, not here:
#   center-for-community-news/student-media-feeds
#
# These are regenerated on every pipeline run and were churning megabytes
# through git nightly. Link-rot preservation is not lost -- the Hub holds every
# article body in stories.parquet, and huggingface/restore_full_text.py
# rehydrates full_text/ from it (fail-closed) at the start of each run.
#
# To get the corpus locally:
#   export HF_REPO_ID="center-for-community-news/student-media-feeds"
#   python huggingface/restore_full_text.py
full_text/
publication_corpora/
bag_of_words.csv
publication_story_index.csv
publication_corpora_manifest.csv

# Hugging Face build artifact — regenerated by huggingface/build_hf_dataset.py
# and pushed to the Hub, never committed here (107MB of copies).
huggingface/dataset_build/

# Contact details, kept out of the published repository.
#
# The committed copies of these files have had every person-identifying column
# removed (names, titles, emails, phone numbers) so the repository can be public.
# The *.private.csv originals keep the full research record locally and must
# never be committed. Nothing in the pipeline reads the dropped columns --
# scripts/geocode_publications.py, the only CI consumer, uses institution,
# state, outlet name, URL and coordinates only.
*.private.csv

# Article bodies for stories deliberately removed from the corpus (the
# professional-outlet exclusions and the Daily Gazette). They were committed to
# full_text/ before the corpus moved to Hugging Face, and HF rebuilds its
# parquet from news_database.csv -- so once full_text/ was purged from git
# history this archive became their only copy. Kept locally, never published.
excluded_full_text_archive.tar.gz
